## Option 3: Simple Provider-Based Integration

### Step 1: Create User Session Provider

```dart
// lib/providers/user_session_provider.dart

final userSessionProvider = StateProvider<UserSession?>((ref) => null);

class UserSession {
  final String email;
  final String userId;
  final String token;

  UserSession({
    required this.email,
    required this.userId,
    required this.token,
  });
}
```

### Step 2: Update dashboard_page.dart for Riverpod

```dart
Future<void> _getUserSessionFromAndroid() async {
  try {
    final result = await platform.invokeMethod<Map>('getUserSession');

    if (result != null) {
      final email = result['email'] as String?;
      final userId = result['userId'] as String?;
      final token = result['token'] as String?;

      if (email != null && userId != null && token != null) {
        // Update provider
        ref.read(userSessionProvider.notifier).state = UserSession(
          email: email,
          userId: userId,
          token: token,
        );

        // Fetch dashboard data
        await ref.read(dashboardProvider.notifier).fetchDashboard(
          userId: userId,
          token: token,
        );
      }
    }
  } on PlatformException catch (e) {
    // Error handling
  }
}
```

